dafdef:Property_n_4923CC6041BF46bfA85D7EFEEEDE5EFB
    a dafm:PropertyDefinition ;
    rdfs:label "RACI" ;
    dafm:eaGuid "{4923CC60-41BF-46bf-A85D-7EFEEEDE5EFB}" ;
    dafm:sourceDatatype "String" ;
    dafm:typingStatus dafm:ExplicitPrimitiveType ;
    dafm:isDerived false ;
    dafm:projectionPredicate dafp:dStakeholder__RACI ;
    rdfs:comment "A RACI responsibility matrix defines roles and responsibilities across a project or process by categorizing tasks into four key areas. Here's a breakdown of each role:\n\nResponsible (R):\nThe person or group performing the task or activity.Directly responsible for completing the work.They take action to accomplish the assigned task.There must be at least one responsible party per task.\n\nAccountable (A):\nThe person or group ultimately answerable for the task’s completion.\nThey delegate and oversee the work performed by the responsible party.Holds the authority to make final decisions.Only one individual is accountable for each task.\n\nConsulted (C):\nSubject matter experts who provide input before the task is completed.\nThey are actively involved by giving advice and feedback.\nTwo-way communication is needed between consulted and responsible parties.\n\nInformed (I):\nIndividuals or groups that need to be kept updated on the progress or outcome.They are not directly involved in the task but need awareness of results.Typically, this is one-way communication." ;
    dafm:minimumCardinality "1" ;
    dafm:maximumCardinality "1" ;
    dafm:defaultValue "I" .

daf:dStakeholder dafm:hasPropertyDefinition dafdef:Property_n_4923CC6041BF46bfA85D7EFEEEDE5EFB .

dafp:dStakeholder__RACI
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "RACI" ;
    rdfs:domain daf:dStakeholder ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    rdfs:comment "A RACI responsibility matrix defines roles and responsibilities across a project or process by categorizing tasks into four key areas. Here's a breakdown of each role:\n\nResponsible (R):\nThe person or group performing the task or activity.Directly responsible for completing the work.They take action to accomplish the assigned task.There must be at least one responsible party per task.\n\nAccountable (A):\nThe person or group ultimately answerable for the task’s completion.\nThey delegate and oversee the work performed by the responsible party.Holds the authority to make final decisions.Only one individual is accountable for each task.\n\nConsulted (C):\nSubject matter experts who provide input before the task is completed.\nThey are actively involved by giving advice and feedback.\nTwo-way communication is needed between consulted and responsible parties.\n\nInformed (I):\nIndividuals or groups that need to be kept updated on the progress or outcome.They are not directly involved in the task but need awareness of results.Typically, this is one-way communication." .

